    {% endif %}
  {% endif %}
  {%- comment -%}
    ═══ PRODUCT TITLE BUDGET — added 2026-08-19 ═══
    Measured on the live sitemap: 23 of 90 titles exceeded 60 chars, worst at
    102, and every worst offender was a PRODUCT page. The cause was
    compositional, not per-product — so it is fixed once, here, rather than by
    editing 23 product records that would drift again with the next 23 products.

    Product titles are ALREADY bilingual ("English Name | العربية"), roughly
    55 chars on their own. This line then appended two more segments:
        " | {condition}"            ~16 chars
        " | Lbass Original المغرب"   ~23 chars
    which is how a 55-char title became 102.

    What changed:
      • CONDITION dropped from <title>. It still renders on the page and in the
        Product schema, which is where it belongs — in a SERP it displaces the
        buying term for a detail the shopper cannot act on before clicking.
      • Brand suffix shortened to " | Lbass" (8 chars, was 23).
      • Hard cap only as a last resort, so the Arabic half survives: the report
        notes Arabic glyphs render narrower than Latin, so ≤60 is a working
        target and a bilingual title may run slightly longer before it cuts.

    An explicit global.title_tag still overrides all of this — see the
    seo_title branch above. This is only the fallback.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign t_base = safe_product_title | strip -%}
