  {%- comment -%}
    ═══ PRODUCT META DESCRIPTION BUDGET — added 2026-08-19 ═══
    Measured: 8 of 90 descriptions exceeded 155 chars, worst at 173, and 6 of
    the 8 were products. Same compositional cause as the title rule above — it
    opened with the FULL bilingual product title (~55 chars) and then appended
    five more clauses.

    Two changes:
      • Opens with the short (first-segment) product name instead of repeating
        the whole title. The title already sits directly above the description
        in a SERP; repeating it spends the snippet on words the user just read.
      • States the ACTUAL shipping prices. The old copy said only
        "التوصيل لكل المغرب" — no figures. The report's whole CTR argument is
        that the COD and price hooks must survive the truncation point, so the
        numbers now sit inside the budget rather than past it.

    Falls back to a shorter form if the composed string still exceeds 155,
    which can happen with a long size value.
  {%- endcomment -%}
