{% comment %}
  ROBOTS — empty collections are noindex,follow.

  Measured 2026-08-05: 11 collections have 0 products. Two of them (women,
  kids) carry fully authored SEO titles and descriptions promising sneakers,
  jackets and hoodies, and both render "ما كاينش منتجات دابا فهاد القسم."
  That is a page that ranks on a promise it cannot keep — the fastest way to
  earn a thin-content impression and a bounce.

  noindex,follow (not nofollow, not a redirect, not deletion): the page keeps
  working for anyone who lands on it, keeps passing link equity onward, and
  returns to the index automatically the moment a product is added — because
  this is computed from live products_count, not a manual flag. Nothing to
  remember to undo.
{% endcomment %}
{%- comment -%}
  2026-08-05 — INTERNAL BUCKETS ARE NOW NOINDEX TOO.

  These utility collections stay reachable but should not compete with the
  customer-facing category URLs in search:

    frontpage               Shopify's default "Home page" collection. Referenced
                            in this theme only inside `unless` guards, i.e. only
                            ever EXCLUDED — nothing renders from it. Its URL is
                            pure duplicate content.

    audited-drop-p001-p012  Customer-facing merchandising view that mirrors the
                            full catalogue. Keep it noindex,follow because its
                            product set intentionally duplicates /collections/all.
  WHY THIS ONLY HALF-SOLVES THE PROBLEM: Shopify auto-generates sitemap.xml from
  everything published to the Online Store channel, and a theme cannot exclude a
  URL from it. So these stay listed in sitemap_collections_1.xml while telling
  Google not to index them — a contradictory signal.

  The complete fix is to UNPUBLISH the empty ones from the Online Store channel
  so they leave the sitemap. That is an owner action — publishableUnpublish is
  blocked for this integration. See the owner-confirmation list.

  noindex,follow (never nofollow): these pages keep passing equity onward, and
  the empty ones return to the index automatically when stocked, because that
  branch is computed from live products_count rather than a manual flag.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign noindex_handles = 'frontpage,audited-drop-p001-p012' | split: ',' -%}
